Core Technical Pillars
Zero Copyright Strike Architecture: Extracting raw audio clips from YouTube interview channels triggers Content ID matches. The engine bypasses this completely by extracting only the text transcript, processing it through an LLM, and re-synthesizing it with Kokoro-82M TTS. Because the output audio waveform is 100% freshly synthesized, automated systems will not flag it as stolen media.

Music Style Matching (Suno Pro): Tailored specifically for driving, high-energy Goa/Ajja-style psytrance (145 BPM, rolling basslines, squelchy acid leads, and hypnotic pads).

Execution Stack:

Transcription & Diarization: WhisperX + pyannote.audio (local CUDA GPU acceleration).

Script Refinement: DeepSeek API (deepseek-v4-flash) at ~$0.0001 per run.

Voice Generation: Kokoro-82M (100% free, local 82-million parameter TTS model).

Video Rendering: FFmpeg (Mandelbrot fractal zoom, .srt subtitle burning, and audio track mixing).

